    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "Stiffness in the axial or limb muscles resulting in an impaired gait, in combination with episodic spasms; improvement with GABA-enhancing medications such as diazepam; continuous motor unit activity on EMG; anti-GAD antibodies support the diagnosis when present",
      "quote": "Stiffness in the axial or limb muscles resulting in an impaired gait, in combination with episodic spasms (often provoked by sudden movement, noise or emotional upset) are generally required to make the diagnosis. Improvement with GABA-enhancing medications such as diazepam and continuous motor unit activity on EMG are expected as well. Symptoms should not be better explained by another condition. The presence of antiGAD antibodies is not required but supports the diagnosis when present.",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
